{"repo":"brokkai/bifrost-dev","kind":"issue","number":11662,"title":"Rust taint: an unrelated finding is silently lost when another procedure reads a tuple field in a sink (depends on procedure name order)","body":"## Summary

In one Rust workspace, an unrelated procedure (`control_plain`) loses its taint finding when another procedure reads a struct tuple field in a sink (`sqlx::query(acc.0.as_str())`). The lost finding is not reported as incomplete: the run's diagnostics name only the procedure with the tuple-field read. The loss depends on the NAME of that other procedure: it happens when the name sorts before `control_plain` (`aaa_case`) and not when it sorts after (`zzz_case`). Source order does not matter. Reading the same field through a method (`acc.text()`) does not lose the finding.

This looks like a silent false negative in a parity-relevant shape (struct wrappers around tainted strings read as `.0`). I have not found the cause and have not tried to fix it.

## Binary

`/mnt/nvme/tmp/85e2d8a9/shared/[redacted]/bifrost` (master 3fa0cc5310, measure profile, sha256 prefix 12f09ed55e925b50). Not yet checked on af9e9a2846.

## Reproduction

Fixtures and outputs are under `/mnt/nvme/tmp/85e2d8a9/tuple-field-order-loss/` (this host only): `aaa-tuple-field/`, `aaa-text-method/`, `o1/`, `o2/`, `run-fixture.sh`. Each fixture holds `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `policies/phone-to-sqlx.rqlp` (source: calls to `get_phone_number`; sink: argument 0 of `sqlx::query`) and the `sqlx` and `String::as_str` packs under `.bifrost/semantic-models/`.

Run, in a copy of the fixture directory, with `[redacted]=1 [redacted]=on BIFROST_PARALLELISM=1 RAYON_NUM_THREADS=1` and fresh cache roots:

    bifrost --root . --no-builtin-policies --policy-file policies/phone-to-sqlx.rqlp --evaluation-date 2026-10-02 --fail-on never --format json

`src/lib.rs` of the failing case (`aaa-tuple-field`):

    pub fn get_phone_number() -> String {
        return String::from("1234567890");
    }

    pub fn control_plain() {
        let q = get_phone_number();
        let _ = sqlx::query(q.as_str());
    }

    pub struct Acc(String);
    pub fn aaa_case() {
        let acc = Acc(get_phone_number());
        let _ = sqlx::query(acc.0.as_str());
    }

## Observed

| case | findings | completion | diagnostics |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `aaa_case` reads `acc.0.as_str()` | 0 (expected: `control_plain` line 7) | inconclusive, partial_discovery | call `from` unresolved; `procedure semantics for ...aaa_case is unknown` |
| same, but `aaa_case` reads `acc.text()` (`impl Acc { fn text(&self) -> &str { &self.0 } }`) | 1 (line 7) | inconclusive, partial_discovery | model-incomplete note for the `control_plain` path; call `from` unresolved; `...aaa_case is unknown` |
| `acc.0.as_str()` procedure renamed `zzz_case` | 1 (line 7) | inconclusive | `...zzz_case is unknown` |
| `acc.0.as_str()` procedure defined first in the file but named `zzz_case` (`o1`) | 1 (line 13) | inconclusive | |
| `acc.0.as_str()` procedure defined last but named `aaa_case` (`o2`) | 0 | inconclusive | |

Compiled endpoints are the same in all cases (2 sources, 2 sinks).

## Expected

`control_plain` has nothing to do with `aaa_case`; its finding must not depend on another procedure's name or on whether that procedure's own analysis is unknown. If a finding is dropped, the run should say so.

## Notes

- Found while writing tests for operator-result typing (the first fixture lost every finding when a tuple-field sink was added).
- Not related to the `+` operator work; no operators appear in the repro.
