{"repo":"brokkai/bifrost-dev","kind":"issue","number":11786,"title":"Rust inactive cfg(any()) module makes an unrelated alias lookup Incomplete","body":"An inactive Rust module makes an otherwise resolvable local type alias lookup report `Incomplete` with `Raw UnsupportedSemantic`. The lookup still returns the single correct candidate `staged_receipt.types.R`, but the residual proof cannot expand it and returns `None` instead of `Some(Unit)`.

This is reproduced on master `[redacted]` with only the portable test and test-only diagnostics added (`[redacted]`). It also reproduces on the #11306 candidate (`fe90c8439c`). Thus #11306 exposed this existing precision bug; it did not introduce it. Selected and fresh answers agree: both are `None`, and their equality assertions pass. The failing assertion is the final positive `Some(Unit)` expectation.

The intended behavior is that `#[cfg(any())] mod inactive;` contributes no active resolution obligation. The unaffected `use facade::R` should resolve completely, and `Result<T, ()>` should prove the unit error. Scope inactive code out while retaining typed incompleteness for actual semantic gaps.

